<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ str_replace('_', '-', app()->getLocale()) }}"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Learn about diabetes · DiaCare</title><x-theme-script /><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.bunny.net"><link href="https://fonts.bunny.net/css?family=instrument-sans:400,500,600,700,800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />@vite(['resources/css/app.css', 'resources/js/app.js'])</head><body class="landing-page"><header class="landing-nav"><a href="{{ url('/') }}" class="landing-brand"><span class="brand-mark">✦</span><span>DiaCare</span></a><nav><a href="{{ route('welcome') }}">Home</a><a href="#basics">Basics</a><a href="#routine">Daily routine</a><x-theme-toggle /><a class="landing-link" href="{{ route('login') }}">Log in</a><a class="landing-cta" href="{{ route('register') }}">Sign up</a></nav></header><main class="learning-page"><section class="learning-hero"><div><span class="landing-kicker">A beginner-friendly guide</span><h1>Learn diabetes<br><em>one idea at a time.</em></h1><p>This guide gives simple background information for everyday tracking. It is educational and does not replace advice from a qualified healthcare professional.</p></div><div class="learning-hero-note"><span>✦</span><strong>Start with what you want to understand.</strong><small>Glucose · Food · Activity · Medication</small></div></section><section id="basics" class="learning-sections"><article class="learn-topic"><span class="topic-number">01</span><div><h2>What is glucose?</h2><p>Glucose is a type of sugar in the blood that the body uses for energy. A glucose reading is a measurement taken at a particular time, so the context and time of the reading matter when looking for patterns.</p><details><summary>Why can readings change?</summary><p>Meals, activity, stress, illness, sleep, medication, and the time of day can all affect glucose. One reading is a snapshot; several readings over time can show a more useful pattern.</p></details></div></article><article class="learn-topic"><span class="topic-number">02</span><div><h2>Food and energy</h2><p>Food provides energy and nutrients. Carbohydrates are broken down into glucose, while protein, fat, fiber, portion size, and the combination of foods can affect how quickly a meal is digested.</p><details><summary>How can meal photos help?</summary><p>A meal photo can help you remember what you ate and estimate nutrition. AI estimates are not exact measurements, especially when ingredients and portion sizes are not visible.</p></details></div></article><article id="routine" class="learn-topic"><span class="topic-number">03</span><div><h2>Activity and routine</h2><p>Activity uses energy and can be part of a person’s diabetes care routine. Recording the type and duration of activity helps you notice how your routine connects with your other records.</p><details><summary>Why record the time?</summary><p>Time helps you compare activity, meals, medications, and readings in the right order. DiaCare automatically records most entries using your current local time.</p></details></div></article><article class="learn-topic"><span class="topic-number">04</span><div><h2>Medication reminders</h2><p>Medication schedules can help you remember when a dose is planned. DiaCare can show reminders for saved schedules, but it does not decide medication doses or tell you to start, stop, or change a medicine.</p><details><summary>What if I miss a dose?</summary><p>Follow the instructions given by your healthcare professional or the medicine label. If you are unsure, contact a pharmacist or clinician rather than guessing.</p></details></div></article></section><section class="learning-disclaimer"><strong>Important</strong><p>DiaCare is for personal tracking and general education. If you have severe symptoms or an urgent concern, seek appropriate medical help. For personal targets and treatment decisions, speak with your healthcare team.</p></section></main><footer class="landing-footer"><div class="landing-brand"><span class="brand-mark">✦</span><span>DiaCare</span></div><a href="{{ route('welcome') }}">Back to home</a><span>© {{ date('Y') }} DiaCare</span></footer></body></html>
